ef 17592186507413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078490 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186507453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078490 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186507478 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078490 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186507479 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078490 #edb/ref 1039 "Removing a Jump Discontinuity in a Piecewise Exponential Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078490 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186078334 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078490 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e155cb07-8d89-5d4b-9015-f73300bab2e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186079397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1045 "Removing Jump Discontinuities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186079227 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1050 660.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186078661 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "c69d16f5-44d0-5069-b44e-d2caf86ea506" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079012 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186076850 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079012 #edb/ref 1069 "q-48583" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079012 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079012 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the function\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{b-3x}+2, & x\\le 0 \\\\ x+3, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis continuous at $x=0$, find the value of the constant $b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079012 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "79180d5f-62ff-58a4-b439-cf96cc9c56ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079012 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=0,$ the left-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}g(x) & =g(0) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{b-3(0)}+2 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{b}+2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nand the right-sided limit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}(x+3) \\\\  & =0+3 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $f(x)$ to be continuous at $x=0,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) \\\\ \\sqrt{b}+2 & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{b} & =3-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{b} & =1 \\\\ b & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079015 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186076868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079015 #edb/ref 1069 "q-48646" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079015 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079015 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the value of the constant $a$ that makes the function $g(x)$ below continuous at $x=2.$\n\n$$\ng(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2ax+1}, & x\\le 2 \\\\ 2x+5, & x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079015 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3e7d303c-6761-5288-b0f2-9a9708133a2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079015 #edb/ref 1074 "At $x=2,$ the left-sided limit is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}g(x) & =g(2) \\\\  & ={3}^{2a(2)+1} \\\\  & ={3}^{4a+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAt $x=2,$ the right-sided limit is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(2x+5) \\\\  & =2(2)+5 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for $g(x)$ to be continuous at $x=2,$ we require that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4a+1} & =9 \\\\ {3}^{4a+1} & ={3}^{2} \\\\ 4a+1 & =2 \\\\ 4a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $g(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$ for $a=\\frac{1}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079227 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079227 #edb/ref 1061 1021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079227 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "778b28a2-a45c-54f3-993a-34eba4c8d1b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079227 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186079683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079228 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079228 #edb/ref 1061 1022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079228 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6bfe194f-fa72-57c9-8918-36cd3025c6c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079228 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079229 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079229 #edb/ref 1061 1025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079229 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "05ececba-94c0-5207-bb02-a5955fd09f40" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079229 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079230 #edb/ref 1061 1027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079230 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "31a192d6-435a-5d0f-9c21-a362b860c2c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079230 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078384 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079397 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186079230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079397 #edb/ref 1061 23595 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079397 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5f820e0e-c43c-5112-8821-d68f8ea15c85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079397 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186078490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079683 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the function $f(x)$ below:\n![](images/e4/e46fcaf79d93513c8b946de51ef451ad8a638936681ce3fc70ffdbe8de023078.svg)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ seems to have a jump discontinuity at $x=-3.$ However, by selecting a particular value for $k$, we can remove the jump discontinuity and make the function continuous.\n\nWe can find this value of $k$ by forcing the left and right-sided limits of the function to be equal at $x=-3\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\lim\\limits_{x\\to (-3)^-} f(x) = \\lim\\limits_{x\\to (-3)^+} f(x)\n$$\n\nFor the left limit, we have,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}(3{x}^{2}+kx) \\\\  & =3(-3)^{2}+k(-3) \\\\  & =27-3k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for the right limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}{x}^{3} \\\\  & =(-3)^{3} \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the left and right limits as equal, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27-3k & =-27 \\\\ 3k & =54 \\\\ k & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, to make $f(x)$ continuous at $x=-3,$ we need to choose $k=18.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079683 #edb/ref 1065 543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079683 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "10dabe2c-998a-5731-bcf2-c0ed93bc7f2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186079683 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506678 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506678 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506678 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "002f9002-0b3a-512a-a5b5-9c9c705ffcd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506681 #edb/ref 1080 "a=-2,\\,b=0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506681 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506681 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01fdf315-e917-535a-a671-e4e9d1962c56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506696 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506696 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506696 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b1751bc-d2e6-59da-9144-c493d8c0547c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506699 #edb/ref 1080 "a=\\frac{1}{2},\\,b=\\frac{2}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506699 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506699 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c822341-4e56-50fd-ba09-fc792dcce56b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506711 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506711 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506711 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "11021f74-53a3-5d6a-920a-dd13858421a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186506717 #edb/ref 1080 "a=0,\\,b=6"